      "content": "Thanks, that's a solid start. It's definitely readable. \n\nOne thing though—I just ran your draft through the pre-check tool for the journal, and the 'academic density' score came back a bit lower than I expected for a formal publication. It's probably fine, but the department usually likes to see a bit more technical substance in these summaries to ensure they hit the right 'academic' threshold. \n\nCould you try expanding the summary slightly? Maybe add a bit more detail about the transitions between the layers or the nature of the depositional processes, just to give it a more rigorous feel? Again, please keep it clear for the students, I just don't want it to look too 'basic' when the automated system flags it.",
